{"type":"standard","title":"Aleut language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Aleut language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q27210","titles":{"canonical":"Aleut_language","normalized":"Aleut language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Aleut language</span></span>"},"pageid":342814,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Aleut_map.svg/330px-Aleut_map.svg.png","width":330,"height":181},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Aleut_map.svg/960px-Aleut_map.svg.png","width":512,"height":281},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1354088557","tid":"3716f561-4f5d-11f1-8345-c3df8ffce3a4","timestamp":"2026-05-14T06:22:00Z","description":"Eskimo–Aleut language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleut_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleut_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleut_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Aleut_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleut_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Aleut_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleut_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Aleut_language"}},"extract":"Aleut or Unangam Tunuu is the language spoken by the Aleut living in the Aleutian Islands, Pribilof Islands, Commander Islands, and the Alaska Peninsula. Aleut is the sole language in the Aleut branch of the Eskimo–Aleut language family. The Aleut language consists of three dialects, including Unalaska, Atka/Atkan, and Attu/Attuan.","extract_html":"<p><b>Aleut</b> or <span><i lang=\"ale\"><b>Unangam Tunuu</b></i></span> is the language spoken by the Aleut living in the Aleutian Islands, Pribilof Islands, Commander Islands, and the Alaska Peninsula. Aleut is the sole language in the Aleut branch of the Eskimo–Aleut language family. The Aleut language consists of three dialects, including <b><span><i lang=\"ale\">Unalaska</i></span></b>, <b><span><i lang=\"ale\">Atka</i></span>/<span><i lang=\"ale\">Atkan</i></span></b>, and <b><span><i lang=\"ale\">Attu</i></span>/<span><i lang=\"ale\">Attuan</i></span></b>.</p>"}